# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model weights and converted binaries -- NEVER COMMIT THESE.
#
# yoloface_8n is GPL-3.0; arcface_w600k_r50 and inswapper_128 are Non-Commercial;
# hyperswap_1a_256 is ResearchRAIL (see docs/model-audit.md).  The converted *_v79.bin
# context binaries are derived works of those weights and carry the same terms.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
work/models/
work/onnx/
work/calib/
# ** and not *: `work/device/*.bin` matches ONE level only, so a subdirectory of context
# binaries -- e.g. work/device/shipped_v79/, the backup convert.sh's in-place overwrite
# makes necessary -- was NOT ignored, in a public repo, for licensed weights.
work/device/**/*.bin
work/device/**/*_net.json
# ncnn model files are derived from the same weights the .bin rule protects: the
# .bin was already ignored, the .param -- the graph topology -- was not.
work/device/**/*.ncnn.param
# The backup of what is HOSTED -- convert.sh overwrites work/device/<name>_v79.bin in
# place, so without this the shipped build is one rebuild away from being unrecoverable.
work/device/shipped_v79/
work/device/io/
work/device/out/
work/device/prof/
work/device/raw/
work/device/ffswap
work/output/

# Qualcomm QAIRT SDK runtime -- proprietary, redistributed only with the SDK licence.
work/android/app/src/main/jniLibs/
work/android/app/src/main/cpp/include/

# Upstream FaceFusion clone; it has its own repository.
# LEADING SLASH IS LOAD-BEARING: an unanchored `src/` matches a directory of that name at
# ANY depth, which silently excluded the entire app source under work/android/app/src/.
/src/

# Test media pulled from facefusion-assets
work/assets/

# Build output
work/android/build/
work/android/app/build/
work/android/app/.cxx/
work/android/.gradle/
work/android/local.properties
work/native/*.so
work/native/libffcv.so
*.apk

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Working notes -- kept on disk, kept OUT of the repository.
#
# CLAUDE.md, HANDOFF.md, docs/ and notes/ are the engineering record: measured numbers,
# dead ends, the 20 traps this port learned, and the session history.  They stay complete
# and current LOCALLY -- they are how the next session picks the work up -- but they are
# not part of the public face of the project.
#
# Untracked, not deleted.  `git rm --cached` was used, so every file is still here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CLAUDE.md
HANDOFF.md
docs/
notes/

# README.md is the EXCEPTION: it is the public face of the project and is tracked. The
# internal one it replaced lives at docs/README-internal.md, which is ignored above.

# Personal launcher; carries account names and profile paths.
claude-yolo.bat

# Generated by convert.sh, and machine-specific by construction: the backend config embeds
# an ABSOLUTE path to its matching htp_config_*.json, because QNN resolves it at conversion
# time. The htp_config_*.json files stay tracked -- they are just arch and VTCM.
work/qnn/htp_backend_*.json

# Release signing. The keystore is NOT recoverable -- back it up somewhere safe. If it is
# lost, no future build can ever update an already-installed app.
work/android/*.jks
work/android/keystore.properties
